{"name":"Mata Hari","hex":"#544859","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mata Hari","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any exotic female spy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mata_Hari"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mata Hari","blocks":[{"text":"Margaretha Geertruida MacLeod, better known by the stage name Mata Hari, was a Dutch exotic dancer and courtesan who was convicted of being a spy for Germany during World War I. She was executed by firing squad in France."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/MataHari15.jpg/330px-MataHari15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mata_Hari","wikidata":"Q82180"},{"title":"Mata Hari (Wildhorn musical)","blocks":[{"text":"Mata Hari at the Moulin Rouge is a musical with a book by Ivan Menchell, lyrics by Jack Murphy, and music by Frank Wildhorn. It is based on the life of Mata Hari, a dancer and spy during World War I."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mata_Hari_(Wildhorn_musical)","wikidata":"Q21998222"},{"title":"Hari","blocks":[{"text":"Hari is among the primary epithets of the Hindu preserver deity Vishnu, meaning 'the one who takes away' (sins). It refers to the one who removes darkness and illusion, the one who removes all obstacles to spiritual progress."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Wood_painting_2%2C_Crafts_Museum%2C_New_Delhi%2C_India.jpg/330px-Wood_painting_2%2C_Crafts_Museum%2C_New_Delhi%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hari","wikidata":"Q2528142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Louise_Jeanne_Mac_Leod.jpg/120px-Louise_Jeanne_Mac_Leod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/Louise_Jeanne_Mac_Leod.jpg?utm_source=en